cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Stability of Matter in Lean: Lieb–Thirring, Ionization, the Thermodynamic Limit and Thomas–Fermi Theory"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of three-dimensional Coulomb stability
  for normalized antisymmetric electron states with finite spin multiplicity
  and static nuclei of bounded nonnegative charge. It proves extended
  additive stability, real quadratic-form stability with Coulomb finiteness,
  kinetic Lieb-Thirring with Rumin's explicit coefficient, Baxter's
  electrostatic inequality with its nearest-other-nucleus correction, and
  the classical Dirichlet-integral meaning of the Fourier kinetic form on
  spin-valued Schwartz functions. Extensions prove the atomic bound
  N < 2Z+1 for weak ground states and strict binding, the neutral
  zero-temperature thermodynamic limit with finite-mass bosonic nuclei
  in Dirichlet balls, and the molecular Thomas-Fermi electronic and total
  energy limits. Thomas-Fermi theory also has a unique relaxed minimizer
  and the exact neutrality threshold for mass saturation and attainment.
